    {
      "id": "HSemxZIwJuEIiP_666Rdl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 76.6328125,
      "y": 160.125,
      "width": 911.5593872070312,
      "height": 950,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0P",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1813380045,
      "version": 1488,
      "versionNonce": 205879469,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786964785349,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Ticketmaster HLD\n\nFunctional requirements\n\nNon functional requirements\n    - CAP theorem ( consistency vs availability on different parts of functional requirements )\n    - Scalability  - handling surges for popular events\n                    - Read >> write \n    - Latency < 5 sec\nOut of scope \n- Complaince - data protection ( GDPR )\n- Fault tolerance\n\n\nData flow\n\nCore entities\n\nAPI\n- Booking in two phases - reserve - lock seat, and confirm.\n\nHigh level design\n    - List down database tables\n        - Relation: one to one, many to many, one to many\n        - pk and fk\n        - Queries\n    - Satisfy all the functional requirements\n\nDeep dive and estimation\n    - show depth at 1 to 3 places.\n        - Elastic search\n        - Redis\n        - CDN\n        - Persistant connection: Http long polling, Websockets, SSE (server sent events)\n        - Virtual waiting queue\n        - Change data capture\n        - Flink Stream processing\n    - Satisfy all non functional requirements.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Ticketmaster HLD\n\nFunctional requirements\n\nNon functional requirements\n    - CAP theorem ( consistency vs availability on different parts of functional requirements )\n    - Scalability  - handling surges for popular events\n                    - Read >> write \n    - Latency < 5 sec\nOut of scope \n- Complaince - data protection ( GDPR )\n- Fault tolerance\n\n\nData flow\n\nCore entities\n\nAPI\n- Booking in two phases - reserve - lock seat, and confirm.\n\nHigh level design\n    - List down database tables\n        - Relation: one to one, many to many, one to many\n        - pk and fk\n        - Queries\n    - Satisfy all the functional requirements\n\nDeep dive and estimation\n    - show depth at 1 to 3 places.\n        - Elastic search\n        - Redis\n        - CDN\n        - Persistant connection: Http long polling, Websockets, SSE (server sent events)\n        - Virtual waiting queue\n        - Change data capture\n        - Flink Stream processing\n    - Satisfy all non functional requirements.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TJ_t1FJz2hGyrmO6jX-rN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -575.6394389706995,
      "y": 585.0445432399137,
      "width": 875.4993896484375,
      "height": 1300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 152889315,
      "version": 1750,
      "versionNonce": 2081695139,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786974489483,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Ticket master\n\nFunctional requirements\n- user should be able to book ticket/seat ( no double booking, seat reserve timeout)\n- select and View events\n    - Event has a performer. Happens at a Venue.\n- Search for events\n\nNon Functional requirements\n- consistency in booking tickets, availability in search and viewing events. ( CAP Theorem)\n- Read >> write, Scalability\n- Handle surges, Scalability\n- Latency < 5 sec ( view and search results )\n\nOut of scope\n- Complaince - GDPR\n- Fault tolerance\n- No UI\n\n\nEntities:\n- Ticket/Seat\n- Booking\n- Event\n- Venue\n- Performer\n- User\n\nAPI\nJWT for user details\n\n- GET /events/\n    {\n        Event,\n        Venue,\n        Performer,\n    }[]\n\n- GET /events/:eventId\n{\n    event,\n    Venue,\n    performer,\n    seats[]\n}\n- POST /book/ticket/reserve { eventId, seat, bookingId }\n    Returns { PaymentDetails }\n- POST /book/ticket/confirm { bookingId } ---> webhook call\n\n- GET /search?term{term}&type{type}&date={date} - Events[]\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Ticket master\n\nFunctional requirements\n- user should be able to book ticket/seat ( no double booking, seat reserve timeout)\n- select and View events\n    - Event has a performer. Happens at a Venue.\n- Search for events\n\nNon Functional requirements\n- consistency in booking tickets, availability in search and viewing events. ( CAP Theorem)\n- Read >> write, Scalability\n- Handle surges, Scalability\n- Latency < 5 sec ( view and search results )\n\nOut of scope\n- Complaince - GDPR\n- Fault tolerance\n- No UI\n\n\nEntities:\n- Ticket/Seat\n- Booking\n- Event\n- Venue\n- Performer\n- User\n\nAPI\nJWT for user details\n\n- GET /events/\n    {\n        Event,\n        Venue,\n        Performer,\n    }[]\n\n- GET /events/:eventId\n{\n    event,\n    Venue,\n    performer,\n    seats[]\n}\n- POST /book/ticket/reserve { eventId, seat, bookingId }\n    Returns { PaymentDetails }\n- POST /book/ticket/confirm { bookingId } ---> webhook call\n\n- GET /search?term{term}&type{type}&date={date} - Events[]\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
